<title>USA: Mirage's Wynn wins $3.1 mln in libel case.</title>
<headline>Mirage's Wynn wins $3.1 mln in libel case.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mirage Resorts Inc Chairman and Chief Executive Officer has won a $3.1 million jury verdict in a libel case centering on the book &quot;Running Scared&quot; by John L. Smith.</p>
<p>In a statement Wynn's attorney, Barry Langberg, said an advertisement for the book alleged Wynn was a &quot;front man&quot; for organized crime.</p>
<p>&quot;The evidence was overwhelming that Mr. Wynn has never had any such ties,&quot; Langberg said.</p>
<p>The Nevada jury awarded Wynn $2.1 million in compensatory damages and $1.073 million in punitive damages.</p>
</text>
